        "original_id": "46b12d63-4a8e-535a-89ef-94b7a854145a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Friends in Low Places\", \"Mr. Blue\", \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\", \"Saturday Night Special\"\n- People: Garth Brooks, Dewayne Blackwell, Larry Bastian, Conway Twitty, David Frizzell\n- Albums: \"No Fences\"\n- Charts: Billboard Top Country Albums\n\nFacts:\n- \"Mr. Blue\" was a 1959 hit song written by Dewayne Blackwell and recorded by the Fleetwoods.\n- \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\" was a 1982 hit song written by Dewayne Blackwell and recorded by David Frizzell.\n- \"Friends in Low Places\" is a song performed by American country pop artist Garth Brooks.\n- \"Friends in Low Places\" was released on August 6, 1990 as the lead single from Garth Brooks's album \"No Fences\".\n- Dewayne Blackwell's songs include \"Friends in Low Places\", which was a 1990 hit for Garth Brooks.\n- \"No Fences\" was released on August 27, 1990.\n- \"No Fences\" reached number 1 on Billboard's Top Country Albums chart.\n- \"Saturday Night Special\" is a song written by Larry Bastian and Dewayne Blackwell and recorded by American country music artist Conway Twitty.",
